<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Julian Grenier</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1275">1275</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Julian of Sidon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Julian Grenier was lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidon">Sidon</a> and Beaufort in the crusader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-jerusalem">Kingdom of Jerusalem</a>. His raid into Mongol-held territory in 1260 provoked a Mongol attack that sacked Sidon. Unable to defend his lands, he sold Sidon and Beaufort to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a>, who held Sidon until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluks</a> took it in 1291.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/julian-grenier.jpg" alt="Julian Grenier" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown. Catalonia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Si%C3%A8ge_de_Sidon_(1260).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
